    <h2>Language and time zone</h2>
    <p>
      The site is written in English, and we respond to inquiries in English. We can also correspond
      in Chinese (中文) where it helps. Our team works China Standard Time (UTC+8), so a message sent
      from Europe or the Americas may receive a reply on the next business day — this is reflected in
      the response expectations below.
    </p>

    <h2>What to include</h2>
    <p>
      A complete inquiry lets us confirm specifications, MOQ, and lead time in the first reply rather
      than asking round after round. Please include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name and company (if any).</li>
      <li>Country / region — so we can discuss documentation, shipping, and any applicable export or
        import requirements correctly.</li>
      <li>Product or ingredient interest.</li>
      <li>Format and target quantity.</li>
      <li>Any specification you already have (aroma profile, dimensions, burn time, packaging, or a
        reference sample).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For a sample or quote, the more specific you are, the more precise the first reply. If you are
      unsure where to start, the <a href="/blog/incense-for-business/">business buying guide</a> and
      the <a href="/blog/oem-private-label-guide/">OEM &amp; private-label guide</a> cover what a
      buyer should prepare before approaching a supplier.
    </p>

    <h2>What happens after you write</h2>
    <p>
      Every inquiry follows the same short path. First, we confirm the specifications and answer the
      direct question — whether a material is available, what the format and MOQ are, and what lead
      time applies. Then, if you proceed, we arrange the next step, which is typically a sample so the
      product can be verified against the written brief before any production commitment. The
      <a href="/blog/samples-program/">samples program</a> page explains how samples work and what to
      evaluate. No figure in any reply is a fixed guarantee — specifications, pricing, MOQ, and lead
      time are confirmed per inquiry and governed by the terms agreed in correspondence.
    </p>

    <h2>Response expectations</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to reply to email and WhatsApp inquiries within <strong>one to two business days</strong>,
      in China Standard Time (UTC+8). Complex commercial briefs — OEM development, multi-format
      quotes, or documentation questions — may take longer, because we confirm specifications, MOQ,
      and lead time against the actual project rather than sending a template reply. If you have not
      heard back after two business days, please follow up: a message occasionally lands in a spam
      folder or a brief goes astray.
    </p>
    <p>
      No figure in a first reply is a fixed guarantee. Prices, MOQs, lead times, and certifications are
      confirmed per inquiry and are governed by the terms agreed in correspondence — see the
      <a href="/terms-of-service/">terms of service</a>. We do not publish fixed MOQ or capacity
      figures because every project differs.
    </p>

    <h2>Commercial inquiries in detail</h2>
    <p>
      Each commercial path has its own starting point, and choosing the right one saves a round trip:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Wholesale</strong> — start from the <a href="/wholesale/">wholesale</a> page, which
        describes the standard product range and the formats available, then email your material,
        format, and quantity.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>OEM</strong> — start from the <a href="/oem/">OEM &amp; Private Label</a> page, then
        email your target aroma profile, format, quantity, packaging, and any specification. We
        confirm sampling, production lead time, MOQ, and documentation per project.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Private label</strong> — start from the <a href="/private-label/">private label</a>
        page, and tell us which existing product you want to re-brand and your packaging requirements.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Samples</strong> — before any production commitment, a sample is normally the next
        step. See the <a href="/blog/samples-program/">samples program</a> page for how it works.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      On all three paths, a buyer should verify the sample against the written brief, agree a
      specification sheet, and request documentation per order rather than assuming certification.
      These checks are spelled out on the <a href="/oem/">OEM</a> and
      <a href="/incense-manufacturer/">manufacturer</a> pages.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial corrections</h2>
    <p>
      To report an error, write to <code>landengltd@gmail.com</code> with the subject "Correction" and
      tell us the page URL and the specific sentence. We correct errors at their source, update the
      page's review date, and — where a dataset is involved — log the change in the dataset changelog.
      We do not silently rewrite, and we do not delete retired entities. This is the same process
      described on our <a href="/blog/landeng-editorial-methodology/">editorial methodology</a> page.
      For a broken link or a changed third-party page, tell us and we will fix or remove it.
    </p>
    <p>
      A note on what a correction is not: we do not revise content because it is unfavourable, and we
      do not remove a correctly sourced entry at a third party's request. A correction is a factual
      fix — an error, a mis-citation, or a genuinely outdated statement — not a request to remove
      accurate information. If you believe a quotation or attribution is misused, tell us and we will
      review it against the source.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <p>To set expectations plainly, we do not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Publish fixed MOQ, capacity, pricing, or certification figures as marketing claims — these
        are confirmed per inquiry.</li>
      <li>Accept unsolicited payments on this site — there is no online ordering or checkout here.</li>
      <li>Add you to a marketing list or newsletter — we send no bulk marketing email.</li>
      <li>Use a contact method other than the three channels listed above.</li>
      <li>Respond to messages requesting medical advice — this site is informational and educational,
        not medical, legal, or financial guidance; see the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.</li>
      <li>Publish customer case studies, testimonials, or "trusted by" logos — we do not fabricate
        commercial social proof.</li>
    </ul>

